  "result": "I fixed it. When a member was removed, `removeMember` passed the role `\"owner\"` into the last-owner check. That check returns immediately when the new role is `\"owner\"`, so it never ran on removals and the last owner could be deleted. Demotions pass the actual lower role, which is why they were still refused.\n\nThe fix is in `src/server/services/member-service.ts`. `assertLastOwnerRetained` now accepts `null` to mean \"the member is being removed\", and `removeMember` passes `null`. With that, removing the last owner is refused the same way demoting them is.\n\nThe type check reported no errors, and the 6 tests in `tests/services/member-service.test.ts` pass, including \"refuses to remove the last remaining owner\". I didn't run the full test suite.\n\nThis stops it happening again but doesn't restore an owner to the organization that already has none. That needs to be done separately.",
